    "physical_description": "Large rectangular garment with a shoulder strap (L. 81.3 cm.) made from two lengths of cloth (223 cm x 66 cm.) stitched along the weft edges \r\nRed ground interrupted by a series of  black, green, white and red coloured warp bands which form a frame for supplementary weft patterning of green; red and white diamonds and yellow zig-zag motifs. These stripes are bisected at intervals (four times), by bands of yellow woven in a diamond twill weave.",
    "summary": null,
    "historical_context": "Fine example of a Chin blanket. (Noel Singer 2003) Traditional costume for the Chin male - it is worn around the body and under the right arm, with the excess tossed over the left shoulder.",
